# tally 2.1.8 S7 (L §7.6 item 6, RUN-LIMIT) over the pairs of a two-stack windows-each diff (item 2): sc and sd
# each state their own dj window, 181 and 180 days, each side's runs under 20 000, their pairs 32 580 over it.
=== m.tally
model pw
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-25
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [a, b]
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place jar[k in ks]: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input amt: money PLN
input dk[k in ks]: date
input dj: date
input dd: int
input d0: date
input amt2: money PLN

move one[k in ks]: transfers
  on dk[k]
  at d0
  leg cash from world to jar[k] amount amt

move two: transfers
  on dj
  at d0
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt2

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dd)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN "s"
  dk[a] = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-10) "s"
  dk[b] = 2026-03-05 "s"
  amt2 = 5.00 PLN "s"
  dd = 10 "s"
  d0 = 2026-01-01 "s"
  dj = window(2026-03-02, 2026-03-04) "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[jar[a]] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[jar[b]] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
ask e8: diff(dj) in sd against sc law 2026-03-01 windows each
=== sc.tally
scenario sc over pw
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

version sc_v
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  replace amt2 = 7.00 PLN "s"
  replace dj = window(2026-01-01, 2026-06-30) "s"
=== sd.tally
scenario sd over pw
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

version sd_v
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  replace dk[b] = 2026-03-07 "s"
  replace dj = window(2026-01-02, 2026-06-30) "s"
=== expect
e8: refused: RUN-LIMIT windows each over more than 20 000 day combinations
